hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1026","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Ismail bin Uwais told us, my brother H told me, Muhammad told us, Ayoub bin Suleiman also told us, he told me Abu Bakr bin Abi Uwais, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Omar bin Muhammad, who is Ibn Zayd, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you prays and does not know how many he has prayed, three or four, let him bow one rak’ah and perform it well.” And he prostrated to it, and he prostrated two prostrations.” Muhammad ibn Yahya said: I found this report in another place in the book of Ayyub, and it has been authenticated. Abu Bakr said: Omar bin Muhammad is the son of Zaid bin Abdullah bin Omar bin Al-Khattab, the brother of Asim, and a leader, and he is the eldest of them. He said: I heard Ahmad bin Saeed Al-Darimi saying: Asim, Omar, Zaid, Waqid, Abu Bakr, and Farqad, these are all brothers. And Asim, who is the son of Muhammad bin Zaid bin Abdullah bin Omar bin Al-Khattab. Abu Bakr said: Al-Darimi told us this after his news."
"1027","And the one who told us, he said: We told him, and the one who told us, he said: Ishaq bin Mansour bin Hayyan told us, Asim Al-Omari told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit said: While Al-Hajjaj was giving the sermon and Ibn Umar was a witness, and with him were two of his sons, one on his right, and the other on his left, when Al-Hajjaj said: Ibn al-Zubayr broke the Book of God, God broke his heart, he said: And Ibn Umar is facing it, so Ibn Umar said: “That one is neither in your hand nor in his hand,” he said: Al-Hajjaj was silent, then he said: God has taught us and every Muslim, and beware of you, O Sheikh, to be wise. So he made Ibn Umar laugh, so he told it on the authority of Asim, On the authority of Habib, he said: Then he jumped up and his two sons made him sit, and he said: “Leave me alone, for I have neglected to say to him: You lied.”"
